      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry to come back to this, but this is not inline with the objectives of the offload. I want to be able to respond the same offload packet for different service names and types. \nThis API does not reflect that. If I imagine how to use this API and want to make the same packet answer for 2 or more different {QNAMES,QTYPES} I\u0027ll do 2 calls with different mServiceNames. Which will result in 2 insertion with the same data, that is bad for memory by design. Do you expect the offload engine to check if the rawpacket is the same for 2 OffloadServiceInfo and merge them behind the scene ?",
